A||||4||vallen11||85 GT keep manual or go automatic?||||5||
Z||000000||vallen11||08-09-2000||12:33 PM||||I need help from the experts?  I have a beautiful two toned '85 GT.  The clutch is bad. I have the 4spd manual. I wonder if I will have problems in the future? The clutch has maybe 50-60k miles on it.  My auto mechanic says it's like $900 for parts and labor and parts to replace clutchy.  He has an 84 automatic Fiero he said he could change it over to an automatic for $1350.  I know I will have to have a new computer chip put in. I just bought a Hypertech chip (works great) which I could trade back in.  My questions are as follows.  What is the chance that I would have problems with the  automatic conversion?  I plan on keeping this car for long time, so would changing it out decrease the collector value of this car? Any info. would be greatly appreciated. YOu can email me direct at vallen@fuse.net||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||08-09-2000||12:47 PM||||You need allot more than a chip change. <P>You need:<P>To wire the torque converter lockup circuit. NOt doing this will kill gas milage and make th tranny run hotter.<P>rewire for a neutral start switch.<P>change brake pedal setup to the correct pedal and remove the clutch pedal. plug the hole left by the clutch master cyl. Add/wire the brake switch for the TC lockup circuit.<P>900$ for parts? sounds awfully high to me. Are those performance part or something? Even then it sounds high.<P>colectability will be hurt, just how much is hard to say. The RPO codes for the car indicate a manual tranny. Collectors like things original most of the time, especially large things like that.<P>There are scads of GM TSB's on the TH125. I'm not sure I'd take one off a 84 4 cyl and stick it on the V6 w/o overhaulling the thing and inspecting certain parts for cracks.<P><p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 08-09-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||vallen11||08-09-2000||12:51 PM||||Hello Ogre,<P>It sounds like a mechanic, who hasn't done one of these might overlook the modifications you just stated.  Since I bought the car about 30,000 miles ago the clutch has always chattered.  If I have the clutch replaced, should I replace the hydraulic system or anything else?  How long should the 4 spd clutch last?||||reg||1
Z||000003||vallen11||08-09-2000||12:54 PM||||One other thing.... while he has the thing torn apart, is there anything that can be done to increase the performance of the car without spending a fortune?||||reg||1
Z||000004||terryk||08-09-2000||03:08 PM||||Leave it manual. I have both (86SE's) and the manual is far more fun. <P>Also, you would need to change the radiator to one with the trans cooler and run the lines to the front of the car.<P>Terry||||reg||1
